	(text "Pin numbers = physical header pins 1-40.  Names = BCM GPIO numbers used in code.\nAll GPIO are 3.3 V logic. Never put 5 V on a GPIO pin.\nUnused pins are marked X (free for future use).\nGPIO19 (pin 35) is reserved by SPI1 as MISO even though the LCD does not use it.\nLCD backlight is on GPIO12 (PWM0) to avoid the GPIO18 / SPI1_CE0 conflict.\n\nFootprint: placeholder 2x20 socket. Swap to the team's\nMODULE_RASPBERRY_PI_ZERO footprint and check the pad numbers match."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 45 174 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "06d91e22-0dec-424f-991d-e567241449c5")
	)
	(text "CS low = SPI mode. R1 pull-up keeps CS high (idle) while the Pi boots.\nSPI mode 0 or 3, clock <= 10 MHz (confirm in datasheet). WHO_AM_I (0x0F) should read 0x6C.\nSDx/SCx (aux bus, unused) tied to GND; OCS_Aux/SDO_Aux left open - verify in datasheet.\nINT1 -> GPIO25 tells the Pi when FIFO data is ready.\nPlace C1 (VDD) and C2 (VDDIO) right next to the chip."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 193 116 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0faf5ea9-643e-45a3-a6dd-a120e7545dae")
	)
	(text "Generated from a design discussion. NOT reviewed - verify every pin against the datasheets before ordering a PCB.\nHow to read this: wires end in NET LABELS. Any two labels with the same name (e.g. SPI0_SCLK) are electrically connected.\nAn X on a pin = intentionally not connected. +3V3 / +5V / GND are power nets shared by everything with that label.\n\nBus plan:  SPI0 (/dev/spidev0.x) = IMU on CE0 + EMG ADC on CE1      SPI1 (/dev/spidev1.0) = LCD\nPi config.txt:  dtparam=spi=on   and   dtoverlay=spi1-1cs"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 20 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "12c007b4-e42a-45c2-aba6-92a71b1f97d0")
	)
	(text "2. IMU - LSM6DSO32 on SPI0, CE0"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 193 42 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1cb54fb8-e548-474d-a160-e14a33bdeb4b")
	)
	(text "3. EMG ADC - MCP3208 on SPI0, CE1"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 193 152 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "33c6aedd-b8ca-40e1-bafa-b3f8f46718ad")
	)
	(text "DRAFT - LHNT EMG: IMU + EMG ADC + LCD on SPI (Raspberry Pi Zero 2 W)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 14 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3df0d0bc-a568-47b8-8b16-be222e9112a4")
	)
	(text "6. Power"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 18 238 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "65ecc683-a263-408e-bfa1-e0f2a93c5d62")
	)
	(text "4. LCD on SPI1"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 310 42 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a1711298-db8f-42ad-b715-6c8abd4eb3ef")
	)
	(text "Pi Zero 2 W has no analog inputs, so the EMG voltage goes through this ADC.\nVREF = 3.3 V  ->  reading 0..4095 = 0..3.3 V.  CH0 = MyoWare ENV, CH1 = RAW.\nMax SPI clock about 1 MHz at 3.3 V: set this speed for spidev0.1 only.\nSupports SPI mode 0 and 3, same as the IMU, so they share the bus fine.\nCH2-CH7 left open for extra EMG channels. Keep EMG traces away from SPI/LCD."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 193 222 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "bd1e37bb-6659-46b4-a2c2-9a29625d5664")
	)
	(text "Generic SPI TFT pinout - reorder J4 to match\nthe module Deetya picks. MISO not used.\nDC = data/command, RST = reset, BL = backlight.\nCheck backlight current vs. the Pi 3.3 V budget.\nIf the LCD driver does not support SPI1,\nswap: LCD -> SPI0, IMU -> SPI1."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 310 82 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d741d124-0505-40c1-bc91-f2bfbb4859a0")
	)
	(text "1. Raspberry Pi Zero 2 W (main controller)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 18 99 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "dd7abf8a-5e80-4ad6-8ebd-c82c94c99215")
	)
	(text "5. EMG sensor - MyoWare"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 310 152 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e2ae2828-1320-42c6-939f-4ba64c0f54a3")
	)
	(text "Powered from 3.3 V so its output never\nexceeds the ADC's 3.3 V reference.\nPin names assume MyoWare 2.0 - check yours.\nElectrodes plug into the MyoWare board itself."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 310 186 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e9f7616f-3d4e-4145-ab90-7fdffbe56227")
	)
	(text "Not included yet: Li-ion charger + protection (e.g. TP4056 + DW01).\nFeeding +5V into header pins 2/4 bypasses the Pi's input protection -\na fuse / reverse-polarity protection is recommended.\nBoost module must handle the Pi's peak current (about 2 A rating to be safe)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25 266 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fc62c5ec-627c-472b-b315-de29bb7fc90b")
	)
